.TH "ROARK\-PHONE\-NUMBER\-CREATE" "1" "" "roark-phone-number-create" "Roark Analytics API Manual"
.SH "NAME"
roark\-phone\-number\-create \- Buy a phone number
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.B roark phone\-number create
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Buys a number from the carrier for this project: the one named by e164, or one Roark picks to match autoPick (trying the next match if the carrier has just sold one). Free inside the plan allowance; past it, the first month of rent is charged now and monthly after that.
.SH "API"
POST /v1/phone\-number
.SH "OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-e164\fR \fI<value>\fR
The number to buy, in E.164 format, from a search result. Give this or autoPick. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pick\fR \fI<value>\fR
What the number Roark picks should look like. Roark buys the first matching number the carrier will sell, preferring the area code and falling back to a nearby one. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pick.country\fR \fI<value>\fR
ISO 3166\-1 alpha\-2 country of the number: US or CA One of: US, CA. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pick.number\-type\fR \fI<value>\fR
LOCAL for a number in an area code, TOLL_FREE for one from the shared US and Canada toll\-free pool One of: LOCAL, TOLL_FREE. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pick.area\-code\fR \fI<value>\fR
Three\-digit area code, or a toll\-free prefix such as 800. When it has no numbers, nearby ones are returned instead, flagged bestEffort. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-auto\-pick.contains\fR \fI<value>\fR
Digits or letters the number must contain (1 to 7, * matches any digit) Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-country\fR \fI<value>\fR
The country of the number given by e164 (default: US). An auto\-picked number uses autoPick.country. One of: US, CA. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-name\fR \fI<value>\fR
A label for the number Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-agent\-id\fR \fI<value>\fR
The agent to assign the number to Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-expect\-free\fR
Whether you expect this number to be free (from the allowance). The purchase is refused with 409 if that has changed since you checked. Optional.
.TP
\fB\-\-expect\-monthly\-rent\-micros\fR \fI<value>\fR
The monthly rent you expect for a paid number, in micros (from the allowance). The purchase is refused with 409 if that has changed since you checked. Optional.
.SH "GLOBAL OPTIONS"
.TP
\fB\-\-data\fR \fI<json>\fR
Request body as JSON, or @file to read one (@\- for stdin).
.TP
\fB\-y\fR, \fB\-\-yes\fR
Skip confirmation prompts.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-input\fR
Never prompt; fail instead.
.TP
\fB\-\-base\-url\fR \fI<url>\fR
API base URL.
.TP
\fB\-\-token\fR \fI<token>\fR
Bearer token. Prefer ROARK_API_BEARER_TOKEN or the stored credential.
.TP
\fB\-\-timeout\fR \fI<ms>\fR
Request timeout in milliseconds.
.TP
\fB\-\-max\-retries\fR \fI<count>\fR
Retries for retryable failures.
.TP
\fB\-\-format\fR \fI<format>\fR
Output format: auto, json, jsonl, plain.
.TP
\fB\-\-json\fR
Shorthand for \-\-format json.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Disable colour.
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress non\-essential output.
.TP
\fB\-\-allow\-project\-base\-url\fR
Send the stored credential to a base URL set by a project .roark.json. Refused by default.
.SH "EXAMPLES"
.PP
.RS 4
.nf
roark phone\-number create
.fi
.RE
